+void SpatiandMediaCodecVideoDecoder::DrawNext() {
+  // A picture drawn while the one before is still in the reader's queue would replace it (the
+  // codec's surface does not wait for the reader): the next is drawn once the reader has given
+  // the one before. Lost so, 60-frame H.264 reached the page at 42 frames a second.
